      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe that\u0027s a matter of preference but in the absence of a need for it to be a single expression, I tend to find the following easier to read than a cascade of logical conditions :\n\n  if (nai.created) return false;\n  // When the agent isn\u0027t already connected when going to the CONNECTED state,\n  // the native network should be created\n  if (state \u003d\u003d CONNECTED) return true;\n  // Otherwise, only create the network upon transitions to CONNECTING.\n  if (state !\u003d CONNECTING) return false;\n  // In U, always create the native network upon transition to CONNECTING.\n  // Before U, keep the legacy behavior to only do this for VPNs.\n  return nai.isVPN() || isAtLeastU();\n\nIn particular because it lets you explain what\u0027s happening.",
